;; ===========================================================================
;; MUST-FAIL FIXTURE (asserted by run-tests.sh: non-zero exit + error grep).
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; This file is the VERBATIM attack that SUCCEEDED against this module during
;; a later change, found by the an internal reviewand reproduced before it was fixed.
;;
;; WHAT IT DID. Making `close-proposal` permissionless (the operator runbook §2.7) meant its gate
;; could no longer be ADMIN, so the swap-and-pop writer was briefly guarded by a
;; `LIFECYCLE` defcap whose body asserted `status = "active"`. That body is a
;; PRECONDITION, NOT AN AUTHORIZATION — it asserts public state an unauthorized caller would need
;; to be true, so it authenticates nobody. A foreign module composed it and called
;; the public `deindex-proposal` directly, skipping the `(>= (curr-time) close-at)`
;; bound that lived only in the close-proposal WRAPPER.
;;
;; MEASURED, attacker holding zero tokens and signing nothing:
;; * a LIVE proposal was popped out of the active index (count 1 -> 0) while
;; `status` stayed "active" and `proposal-active?` stayed true;
;; * the transfer release-loop scans that index, so it went blind;
;; * alice voted 2,500, transferred all 2,500 to dave, dave voted the SAME tokens:
;; final tally yes 5,000 against circulating 2,500 — quorum met, passed true.
;; THE CONTROL THAT MADE IT DECISIVE: the identical foreign route against the
;; PREVIOUS `ADMIN` gate was BLOCKED on the same engine, in the same run. That is
;; what proved it a REGRESSION rather than a pre-existing exposure —
;; `enforce-keyset` authenticates, `status = "active"` does not.
;;
;; WHY IT IS A FIXTURE AND NOT AN `expect-failure`: the fix deleted BOTH
;; `LIFECYCLE` and `deindex-proposal` (the swap-and-pop is now inlined into
;; close-proposal and cancel-proposal, Pattern W applied to a state-transition
;; writer). So both references below are NAME-RESOLUTION failures — they abort the
;; whole file at compile time, which `expect-failure` cannot catch (pact-traps
;; §REPL testing artifacts). The runner asserts it from outside, on the exit code
;; AND the error text.
;;
;; ENGINE-INDEPENDENCE IS THE POINT, and it is the same argument as
;; freemint-compose.repl-must-fail. The bare REPL is pact 5.4 = the PRE-Chainweb32
;; engine, where compose-capability still skips guardForModuleCall — the most
;; permissive engine there is, the one where this attack worked. It dies here
;; anyway, because there is nothing left to call. "Safe because the code says so",
;; not "safe because a closed-source engine says so" (the design record §2.2, reason 3).
;; Do NOT convert this to a fork-gated devnet test, and do NOT re-introduce a named
;; index writer with a precondition-shaped guard.
;; ===========================================================================
(load "setup.repl")

(begin-tx "seed float + a LIVE proposal")
(env-keys ["admin-key"])
(n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.init 0.5)
(n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.resume-sale)
(env-data { "alice": { "keys": ["alice-key"], "pred": "keys-all" } })
(env-sigs [{ "key": "admin-key", "caps": [(coin.TRANSFER "sender00" "alice" 1250.0)] }])
(coin.transfer-create "sender00" "alice" (read-keyset 'alice) 1250.0)
(env-sigs [{ "key": "alice-key", "caps": [(coin.TRANSFER "alice" (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.proceeds-account) 1250.0)] }])
(n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.buy "alice" (read-keyset 'alice) 2500.0)
(commit-tx)

